_at":1786138790,"sha":"396380c640bf0d9164b1a9356201fa181535fc10","subject":"feat(notification-gates): make gate rejections diagnosable and retries deliberate"}],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"chat":{"digest":"cdab761bf6a799c1f92c181fe7d2b9ab281feae6f56fe5877daddf1912365c51","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-h7.1/chat.md","size_bytes":6336},"commits":{"digest":"f9b12fbf651a828b102734828a0ffc84d964daf4db42a511ff1e270821592159","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-h7.1/commits.json","size_bytes":259},"embedded_workflows":{"digest":"a398c70160fe308637edd70b38d8cf02cc697183c480675d10f387d529663058","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-h7.1/embedded_workflows.json","size_bytes":80},"meta":{"digest":"a01466a2ff82c0b9aea6ed1dc5248307b4639faa831d988315bc00b344ebbab4","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-h7.1/meta.json","size_bytes":10076},"prompt":{"digest":"d3c0fd7cd154082875eb1032fdc13d17cb8636dbef35b9fd82392a2524a6920d","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-h7.1/prompt.md","size_bytes":182},"prompt_steps":{"digest":"af58ec45b7bf11c8ff18abafdf0e89f29138a5f4c2854d6746354f49db4d5d4d","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-h7.1/prompt_steps.json","size_bytes":11012},"state":{"digest":"2a60d859645a91967cff0f6f11caefda22a6a308c48faf8c784445561880d406","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-h7.1/state.json","size_bytes":183}},"finished_at":null,"global_name":"bbugyi200.athena.sase-h7.1","local_name":"sase-h7.1","metadata":{"agent_clan":"sase-h7","agent_clan_generation":"20260807171251","approve":true,"bead_id":"sase-h7.1","changespec_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","cl_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","clan_summary":"[bold #D75FFF]◆ EPIC sase-h7[/bold #D75FFF]\n[dim]  Title: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]Gate input collection and repeatable non-terminal gate actions[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]A reviewer can supply typed, validated input to any gate command [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]from every surface, and can run repeatable non-terminal gate [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]actions — starting with `edit_file` — that help them decide without[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]answering the gate. Custom gates that declare required input become[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]answerable instead of silently stuck, the three incompatible [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]feedback rules collapse into one, and the free-text smuggling that [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]snooze and triage rely on is retired.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]12[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]4[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plans:202608/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]gate_input_collection.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202608/gate_input_collection.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-h7[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-h7/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Diagnosable input failures and non-destructive retry[/bold #D7AFFF]          [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]executor-integrity[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]executor-integrity: move gate input-schema validation inside the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]error-recording path, bound input size and depth, and add a per-attempt [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]execution journal so a partially executed AND branch can be resumed or [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]restarted deliberately instead of silently re-running its completed [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]commands.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]One feedback-to-input rule for every surface[/bold #D7AFFF]                  [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]feedback-input[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]feedback-input: replace ACE's never-copy, mobile's option-id heuristic, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and Telegram's required-list heuristic with one shared helper that [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]injects the reviewer's note as `input.feedback` whenever the selected [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]option's schema declares a `feedback` property, after auditing every [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]built-in schema.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Declarative per-option inputs and per-option submission[/bold #D7AFFF]       [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]inputs-core[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]inputs-core: add the closed per-option `inputs:` authoring vocabulary [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]built on `InputArg`/`InputType` (plus a new `enum` type), compile it [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]into the option's `input_schema` at creation, and teach the executor to [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]accept and persist one input value per selected option instead of one [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]shared blob.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Repeatable non-terminal gate actions[/bold #D7AFFF]                          [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]gate-actions[dim] · [dim][/dim]after executor-integrity[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]gate-actions: generalize `operations` into a rendered vocabulary of [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]repeatable actions that never answer the gate — `edit_file` gains [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]presentation and an origin-file edit target, and a new `run_command` [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]kind runs a hashed bundle command whose output is shown to the reviewer.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Fail closed at creation for unanswerable gates[/bold #D7AFFF]                [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]custom-validation[dim] · [dim][/dim]after inputs-core[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]custom-validation: add the missing `kind_validation/custom.py`, reject [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]at creation any option whose effective input schema cannot accept what a[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]client can produce, pin the JSON Schema dialect, and make an omitted [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`input_schema` mean \"no input\" instead of the permissive empty schema.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Generic typed input collection in the ACE gate modals[/bold #D7AFFF]         [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]inputs-ace[dim] · [dim][/dim]after inputs-core[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]inputs-ace: extract the typed-field form out of `InputCollectionModal` [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]into a reusable widget and render each selected option's declared inputs[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]inside `GateBranchControls`, so plan, epic, custom, triage, and snooze [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]gates all collect input with no per-kind code.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Gate actions in the ACE modals and the plan edit round trip[/bold #D7AFFF]   [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]gate-actions-ace[dim] · [dim][/dim]after gate-actions[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]gate-actions-ace: render an Actions section in the shared gate modals, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]run `edit_file` in place without tearing down the modal, point the plan [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and epic edit action at the durable `~/.sase/plans/` file, and block [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]submission while an unaccepted draft exists.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Mobile wire and Telegram step flow for declared inputs[/bold #D7AFFF]        [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]inputs-remote[dim] · [dim][/dim]after feedback-input, inputs-core[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]inputs-remote: extend the frozen `mobile_api_v1` gate contract in [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`sase-core` with declared input fields and per-option submitted values, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]update the Rust request struct, routes, and Python bridge, and add an [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]input step flow to the Telegram gate conversation.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  9 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]sase gate answer, act, and show[/bold #D7AFFF]                               [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]gate-cli[dim] · [dim][/dim]after gate-actions, inputs-core[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]gate-cli: add headless `answer`, `act`, and `show` subcommands to `sase [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]gate` and build the cross-surface conformance fixture matrix that runs [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the same input cases through ACE, the mobile bridge, and the CLI.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  10 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Show the input a gate asks for and the input it received[/bold #D7AFFF]     [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]surface-input[dim] · [dim][/dim]after gate-actions, inputs-core[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]surface-input: render declared and submitted input in the gate detail [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]pane and Gate Debug, and add `input`, `option_inputs`, `option_results`,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and executed actions to `sase gate wait --json`.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  11 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Retire free-text smuggling from snooze, triage, and launch[/bold #D7AFFF]   [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]retire-smuggling[dim] · [dim][/dim]after feedback-input, inputs-ace, inputs-remote[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]retire-smuggling: 